The `traverse` method recursively traverses the DOM tree, applying the selector function and weight adjustments to each element. It collects elements that match the selector into an array.

The `fetchDependencies` method fetches data from external dependencies asynchronously. The `processBatch` method processes a batch of elements, which includes fetching dependencies and performing actions on each element.

The `traverseAndProcess` method orchestrates the traversal and processing of all elements in batches to handle rate limiting and large document fragments efficiently.

The `md5` static method is provided for generating an MD5 hash for a given string input.

