This code defines a `DynamicValueGenerator` class that manages configurable value ranges for both floats and integers, supports inclusive and exclusive bounds, and provides methods to generate random values within these ranges. It also includes methods to log the generated values and handle concurrent generation requests from multiple threads without introducing race conditions or data inconsistencies.

The class uses a `ConcurrentDictionary` to store the configuration of each range, ensuring that any changes to the configuration are seamlessly propagated to all active threads. The class supports dynamic configuration updates, allowing range boundaries to be adjusted at runtime without interrupting ongoing generation processes.

The class also includes methods to track the number of structures with set CRCFLAG and dynamically adjust the probability threshold to maintain the target ratio, even under varying data rates. It handles memory allocation in chunks to minimize fragmentation and provides feedback to the caller on the current state, including the achieved ratio of CRCFLAGs and performance metrics such as memory usage and execution time.

The class supports concurrent access by multiple threads, ensuring thread safety and efficient synchronization mechanisms to prevent race conditions. Memory allocation failures are handled gracefully, and the function provides feedback to the caller on the current state.

Finally, the class integrates with an external hardware device for real-time data acquisition and transmission, using a buffering strategy to handle incoming data packets efficiently, ensuring no loss of critical information. The class implements a robust error recovery mechanism that can detect and recover from temporary connectivity issues.']

